## Questions
- **Q1** — can the whole PLAN be cut? Only when the **Test Strategy** rules its whole feature area out — cite the Test Strategy section. Unsupported TPS rows are not enough to cut a plan: deselect the affected cycles (Q2) or cases (Q3/Q4) instead.
- **Q2** — within the plan, which CYCLES are not relevant? (unsupported feature, device incapable of the test)
- **Q3** — within the cycles, which CASES are not relevant? (the feature is not in the TPS, or the device does not have it)
- **Q4** — of the remaining cases, which test a feature the TPS marks NOT supported on first release (the "NOT supported" list above)?

## Rules
- Use only the keys listed in "The template plan to trim". Q1 names the plan key, Q2 a cycle key, Q3 and Q4 a case key.
- Every deselection needs a short `reason` and a `source` that cites the document and the exact row or section: copy a TPS line from the lists above as it appears, or name the section (`Test Strategy §<number> <title>`, `TPS §<number> <title>`).
- A feature in the UNDECIDED list is never a reason to deselect. Add a note naming the dependency instead.
- If the plan is cut (Q1), do not also list its cycles and cases.
- Do not deselect a test because it is generic, old, or similar to another one — only for the reasons above.
- `notes` are the "AI Notes": short facts from the documents that back up your answers or that the engineer should know about this plan — hardware the device lacks, limits, dependencies — each ending with its source. A note may name a key from the plan.
- If nothing should be deselected, return an empty `deselect` list. That is a normal answer.

## Output — JSON only, this shape:
```json
{"deselect": [{"key": "<a key from the plan>", "question": "<Q1|Q2|Q3|Q4>", "reason": "<one line>", "source": "<document, section or TPS line>"}],
 "notes": [{"key": null, "note": "<one fact> — <source>"}]}
